{"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "formalize", "attempt": 2, "request": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling\n\nImplement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function. Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values. Use Python standard library only, no external I/O. Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end. Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events. For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,... strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)). Sum only non-null in-range values; count counts these values. A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value. Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first); empty buckets never reset previous. Events before start never seed previous. Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order. Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.\n\nImplement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.\n\nPublic examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]\n", "clauses": [{"clause_id": "C1", "quote": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling", "refs": []}, {"clause_id": "C2", "quote": "Implement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C3", "quote": "Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C4", "quote": "Use Python standard library only, no external I/O.", "refs": ["R1"]}, {"clause_id": "C5", "quote": "Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C6", "quote": "Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C7", "quote": "For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C8", "quote": "strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C9", "quote": "Sum only non-null in-range values;", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C10", "quote": "count counts these values.", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C11", "quote": "A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.", "refs": ["I1", "O5"]}, {"clause_id": "C12", "quote": "Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first);", "refs": ["O5"]}, {"clause_id": "C13", "quote": "empty buckets never reset previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C14", "quote": "Events before start never seed previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C15", "quote": "Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C16", "quote": "Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.", "refs": ["I1", "O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C17", "quote": "Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C18", "quote": "Use only the standard library, no external I/O.", "refs": ["R1"]}, {"clause_id": "C19", "quote": "The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C20", "quote": "Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C21", "quote": "Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]", "refs": ["O7"]}], "records": [{"id": "D1", "revision": 1, "kind": "entity", "role": "declaration", "statement": "Input contains events with string group, integer time and integer-or-null value; integer start and end with start<=end; positive integer width; and fill equal to none or previous.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 366, "interpretation": "Input schema and domain.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 238}], "scope": ["input domain"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["Represent the specified input domain without additional restrictions."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:b57d83415b32656ca25440340591b594cc06f9d558995ef297a01a62a851abf4", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O1", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Provide a pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) function in solution.py receiving JSON-compatible Python values and returning a JSON-serializable value.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 134, "interpretation": "File and interface.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 79}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 186, "interpretation": "Value compatibility.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 135}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1129, "interpretation": "Language, purity and determinism.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1053}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1251, "interpretation": "Serialization contract.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1178}], "scope": ["function interface"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["solution.py exposes solve(data) in Python 3.", "Repeated calls with identical input yield identical results.", "The function is pure and returns JSON-serializable output."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:0736df252aaa0fc930a5329b0bc3e757046074a67cd4af398249f8e72f43b78c", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O2", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Enumerate all distinct event group names lexicographically, including groups having no in-range events.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 474, "interpretation": "Complete ordered group enumeration.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 367}], "scope": ["group enumeration"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Groups equal sorted distinct names from all events.", "Null-valued and out-of-range events still establish group membership."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e35fdf86d6d6a5b373c6e6ade04be096bc8b828ff92dab99e42e0ef1ee685284", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O3", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For every group emit buckets starting start+k*width for nonnegative integers k while strictly below end, covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 534, "interpretation": "Bucket progression.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 475}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 610, "interpretation": "Half-open intervals and end boundary.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 535}], "scope": ["bucket enumeration and membership"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Bucket starts are exactly start,start+width,... below end.", "Intervals include their lower endpoint and exclude their upper endpoint.", "The final interval is truncated at end.", "start=end yields no buckets."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:0f07d09fa25e3c9b931227dc4c6666f1541e0aca5fa07b7288d90bf02f572bea", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O4", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For each group and bucket, sum and count precisely the non-null event values within its interval, counting duplicate occurrences separately.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 645, "interpretation": "Sum eligibility.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 611}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 672, "interpretation": "Count eligibility.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 646}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Duplicate multiplicity.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["aggregation"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["count equals the number of eligible event occurrences.", "sum equals their integer sum.", "Null values and out-of-range events contribute neither sum nor count.", "Duplicates contribute separately."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:461c96c328d90bf5ae6a65097cf277570a14d4a9438cf6819b2cd5900ac2354f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O5", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "A bucket with positive count returns its sum. A bucket with zero count returns null for fill none, or the latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous, with null before the first nonempty bucket.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 732, "interpretation": "Nonempty value.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 673}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 852, "interpretation": "Empty value by fill mode.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 733}], "scope": ["bucket output values"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "I1", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Positive count yields value=sum.", "Zero count with fill none yields null.", "Zero count with fill previous yields previous when present, otherwise null.", "Filling leaves count at zero."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:97e93a0893f91961246724bd28bf7b31266d387770c5b061439b76381c491475", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O6", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Return a list of records containing group,start,count,value, ordered by lexicographic group then increasing bucket start, preserving the specified structure.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 992, "interpretation": "Output records and ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 930}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1317, "interpretation": "Structural fidelity.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1252}], "scope": ["output structure and ordering"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O5", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Each emitted bucket produces exactly one record with group,start,count,value.", "Records follow group then bucket order.", "Empty events or start=end produce an empty list."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:6c76eecfc2a21c927d46ab8fedd884cb2ad0cfd19af365f36cecd309fce82537", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O7", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Reproduce both public examples: the a example returns count 2 and value 0 at start 0, then count 0 and value 0 at starts 2 and 4; the z example returns count 0 and null at start 0.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1891, "interpretation": "Required public example outputs; held-out scoring is evaluation context.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1319}], "scope": ["public examples"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O6", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["The first example returns exactly its three specified records.", "The second example returns exactly its single specified record."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:2dd535e56b298af103042290d83c3ffde8242b68dff99de4b5f570000ec35099", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "I1", "revision": 1, "kind": "invariant", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Each group independently starts with no previous sum. Processing a nonempty bucket sets previous to its sum, including zero; processing an empty bucket preserves previous. Events before start never initialize previous.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 732, "interpretation": "Previous update.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 673}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 888, "interpretation": "State persistence.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 853}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 929, "interpretation": "Initial causal boundary.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 889}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Zero is valid state.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["per-group causal fill state"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Before a bucket, previous is the latest earlier nonempty bucket sum or absent.", "After a nonempty bucket, previous equals that bucket's sum.", "Empty buckets preserve previous.", "Zero is retained as a valid previous value.", "Pre-start events cannot seed previous."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:d5086720d1c9352a7466b2889fbba030ed74901f62b6ae55b11ae7209f9877a5", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "R1", "revision": 1, "kind": "resource_constraint", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Use only the Python standard library and perform no external I/O.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 237, "interpretation": "Dependency and I/O constraints.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 187}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1177, "interpretation": "Repeated constraints.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1130}], "scope": ["implementation and invocation"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No third-party dependencies.", "No external I/O."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e06936e6870ce6c82d8d588a499f730b8486e947add48d7a2a937a1342ab0856", "blocked_by": []}], "lean_source": "-- formalizer capability gap (untrusted report)\n", "formalization": {"capability_report": {"encoding": "verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1", "obligation_ids": ["D1", "O1", "O2", "O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "O7", "I1", "R1"], "gaps": [{"obligation_ids": ["O2", "O6"], "feature": "Unicode lexicographic string comparison", "reason": "The required ordering of distinct arbitrary string group names cannot be expressed using the admitted string equality, concatenation, length and emptiness operations. Numeric lt and le do not accept String operands.", "attempted_representations": ["Preserve events as records with group:String, time:Int and value:Option Int. A fold with equality-based filtering can collect distinct names, including those established only by null or out-of-range events, but its traversal order is input order rather than the required lexicographic order.", "An insertion fold requires a comparison between the current group and previously collected groups. Neither length comparison nor equality determines the required order of arbitrary equal-length names. No admitted operation extracts Unicode scalar values for a faithful numeric comparison.", "Encoding group names as caller-supplied scalar lists or requiring sorted events would change the actual String input type or add an unauthorized caller restriction. Raw Lean string ordering remains outside the required executable DSL gates."]}, {"obligation_ids": ["O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "I1"], "feature": "Total integer-controlled bucket sequence generation", "reason": "Bucket starts must enumerate start+k*width below end for arbitrarily large valid integer intervals. The admitted grammar has no range, numeric iterator, recursive definition or conversion from a numeric bound to a list that can generate this sequence.", "attempted_representations": ["For one event establishing a group, start=0 and width=1 require end output records for every positive integer end. Any fixed acyclic composition of folds over that singleton event list and fixed literal lists has a bounded output length independent of end, even when its arithmetic terms compute end.", "Nested folds and list appends can expand existing lists, but their iteration counts still depend on available list lengths rather than the integer interval. Conditional branches can select such constructions but cannot provide an unbounded numeric iteration.", "Once bucket starts exist, a fold with an accumulator containing previous:Option Int and output records can retain zero sums, preserve previous through empty buckets, and initialize previous separately for each group. An inner event fold can compute duplicate-sensitive counts and sums using time guards and option_is_some. This faithfully addresses nulls and causal filling but cannot generate the missing bucket starts.", "Supplying bucket starts as an additional input field, imposing an interval bound, or emitting only buckets represented by events would respectively alter the input structure, restrict the domain, or omit required empty buckets. Raw Lean range construction does not satisfy the same executable DSL acceptance gates."]}]}}, "profile": null, "statements": {}, "diagnostics": [{"code": "UNSUPPORTED_CAPABILITY", "severity": "blocking", "message": "Formalizer reported a capability gap; seek a faithful supported alternate representation without weakening any frozen obligation: {\"encoding\":\"verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1\",\"gaps\":[{\"attempted_representations\":[\"Preserve events as records with group:String, time:Int and value:Option Int. A fold with equality-based filtering can collect distinct names, including those established only by null or out-of-range events, but its traversal order is input order rather than the required lexicographic order.\",\"An insertion fold requires a comparison between the current group and previously collected groups. Neither length comparison nor equality determines the required order of arbitrary equal-length names. No admitted operation extracts Unicode scalar values for a faithful numeric comparison.\",\"Encoding group names as caller-supplied scalar lists or requiring sorted events would change the actual String input type or add an unauthorized caller restriction. Raw Lean string ordering remains outside the required executable DSL gates.\"],\"feature\":\"Unicode lexicographic string comparison\",\"obligation_ids\":[\"O2\",\"O6\"],\"reason\":\"The required ordering of distinct arbitrary string group names cannot be expressed using the admitted string equality, concatenation, length and emptiness operations. Numeric lt and le do not accept String operands.\"},{\"attempted_representations\":[\"For one event establishing a group, start=0 and width=1 require end output records for every positive integer end. Any fixed acyclic composition of folds over that singleton event list and fixed literal lists has a bounded output length independent of end, even when its arithmetic terms compute end.\",\"Nested folds and list appends can expand existing lists, but their iteration counts still depend on available list lengths rather than the integer interval. Conditional branches can select such constructions but cannot provide an unbounded numeric iteration.\",\"Once bucket starts exist, a fold with an accumulator containing previous:Option Int and output records can retain zero sums, preserve previous through empty buckets, and initialize previous separately for each group. An inner event fold can compute duplicate-sensitive counts and sums using time guards and option_is_some. This faithfully addresses nulls and causal filling but cannot generate the missing bucket starts.\",\"Supplying bucket starts as an additional input field, imposing an interval bound, or emitting only buckets represented by events would respectively alter the input structure, restrict the domain, or omit required empty buckets. Raw Lean range construction does not satisfy the same executable DSL acceptance gates.\"],\"feature\":\"Total integer-controlled bucket sequence generation\",\"obligation_ids\":[\"O3\",\"O4\",\"O5\",\"O6\",\"I1\"],\"reason\":\"Bucket starts must enumerate start+k*width below end for arbitrarily large valid integer intervals. The admitted grammar has no range, numeric iterator, recursive definition or conversion from a numeric bound to a list that can generate this sequence.\"}],\"obligation_ids\":[\"D1\",\"O1\",\"O2\",\"O3\",\"O4\",\"O5\",\"O6\",\"O7\",\"I1\",\"R1\"]}", "obligations": ["I1", "O2", "O3", "O4", "O5", "O6"], "claims": [], "details": {"phase": "formalize", "untrusted_report": true, "capability_report": {"encoding": "verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1", "obligation_ids": ["D1", "O1", "O2", "O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "O7", "I1", "R1"], "gaps": [{"obligation_ids": ["O2", "O6"], "feature": "Unicode lexicographic string comparison", "reason": "The required ordering of distinct arbitrary string group names cannot be expressed using the admitted string equality, concatenation, length and emptiness operations. Numeric lt and le do not accept String operands.", "attempted_representations": ["Preserve events as records with group:String, time:Int and value:Option Int. A fold with equality-based filtering can collect distinct names, including those established only by null or out-of-range events, but its traversal order is input order rather than the required lexicographic order.", "An insertion fold requires a comparison between the current group and previously collected groups. Neither length comparison nor equality determines the required order of arbitrary equal-length names. No admitted operation extracts Unicode scalar values for a faithful numeric comparison.", "Encoding group names as caller-supplied scalar lists or requiring sorted events would change the actual String input type or add an unauthorized caller restriction. Raw Lean string ordering remains outside the required executable DSL gates."]}, {"obligation_ids": ["O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "I1"], "feature": "Total integer-controlled bucket sequence generation", "reason": "Bucket starts must enumerate start+k*width below end for arbitrarily large valid integer intervals. The admitted grammar has no range, numeric iterator, recursive definition or conversion from a numeric bound to a list that can generate this sequence.", "attempted_representations": ["For one event establishing a group, start=0 and width=1 require end output records for every positive integer end. Any fixed acyclic composition of folds over that singleton event list and fixed literal lists has a bounded output length independent of end, even when its arithmetic terms compute end.", "Nested folds and list appends can expand existing lists, but their iteration counts still depend on available list lengths rather than the integer interval. Conditional branches can select such constructions but cannot provide an unbounded numeric iteration.", "Once bucket starts exist, a fold with an accumulator containing previous:Option Int and output records can retain zero sums, preserve previous through empty buckets, and initialize previous separately for each group. An inner event fold can compute duplicate-sensitive counts and sums using time guards and option_is_some. This faithfully addresses nulls and causal filling but cannot generate the missing bucket starts.", "Supplying bucket starts as an additional input field, imposing an interval bound, or emitting only buckets represented by events would respectively alter the input structure, restrict the domain, or omit required empty buckets. Raw Lean range construction does not satisfy the same executable DSL acceptance gates."]}]}}}], "previous_critique": {"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "formalize", "attempt": 1, "status": "REPAIR", "tiers": [{"tier": "R0", "members": 1, "accepts": 0, "rejects": 1, "abstains": 0, "missing": [], "blocking_findings": ["critic/formalize/1/R0/group-1/critic/1"], "result": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "reasons": ["unresolved blocking findings veto: critic/formalize/1/R0/group-1/critic/1"]}], "results": [{"tier": "R0", "agent": "critic", "instance": "critic/formalize/1/R0/group-1/critic/1", "proposal": {"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "verdict": "REPAIR", "counterexamples": [], "corrections": [{"diagnostic_index": 0, "artifact": "formalization.json", "explanation": "Retain the negative capability report: no faithful alternate is available in the supplied grammar. O2/O6 require Unicode lexicographic comparison; equality, concatenation, length and emptiness permit deduplication but cannot implement arbitrary string ordering. O3 requires an integer-controlled range or total numeric iteration primitive. With one event establishing a group, start=0, width=1 and arbitrarily large end require arbitrarily many output records; folds over existing lists and fixed literal lists cannot generate this independently of input list lengths. Option Int faithfully represents null and zero-valued previous sums and permits causal state updates once bucket starts exist, but does not supply either missing primitive. Preserve every active obligation and the exact input/output types; do not add presorted-input assumptions or a caller-provided bucket list. Raw Lean remains subject to the same executable-DSL gates, so it does not establish a supported fix. This report remains untrusted and blocked, with no executable implementation to counterexample."}]}, "checked": null, "status": "REPAIR"}], "feedback": ["CRITIC DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR: Retain the negative capability report: no faithful alternate is available in the supplied grammar. O2/O6 require Unicode lexicographic comparison; equality, concatenation, length and emptiness permit deduplication but cannot implement arbitrary string ordering. O3 requires an integer-controlled range or total numeric iteration primitive. With one event establishing a group, start=0, width=1 and arbitrarily large end require arbitrarily many output records; folds over existing lists and fixed literal lists cannot generate this independently of input list lengths. Option Int faithfully represents null and zero-valued previous sums and permits causal state updates once bucket starts exist, but does not supply either missing primitive. Preserve every active obligation and the exact input/output types; do not add presorted-input assumptions or a caller-provided bucket list. Raw Lean remains subject to the same executable-DSL gates, so it does not establish a supported fix. This report remains untrusted and blocked, with no executable implementation to counterexample."], "diagnostics": [], "milestone_authority": false, "snapshot_ref": {"path": "agents/memory/snapshots/00000009-e6020b0fa25a3a197c03a9588e0c116e19458a250210323aa0b992f11e5b1d50.json", "sha256": "sha256:e6020b0fa25a3a197c03a9588e0c116e19458a250210323aa0b992f11e5b1d50", "size": 692}}, "raw_formalizer_response": "{\"encoding\":\"verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1\",\"obligation_ids\":[\"D1\",\"O1\",\"O2\",\"O3\",\"O4\",\"O5\",\"O6\",\"O7\",\"I1\",\"R1\"],\"gaps\":[{\"obligation_ids\":[\"O2\",\"O6\"],\"feature\":\"Unicode lexicographic string comparison\",\"reason\":\"The required ordering of distinct arbitrary string group names cannot be expressed using the admitted string equality, concatenation, length and emptiness operations. Numeric lt and le do not accept String operands.\",\"attempted_representations\":[\"Preserve events as records with group:String, time:Int and value:Option Int. A fold with equality-based filtering can collect distinct names, including those established only by null or out-of-range events, but its traversal order is input order rather than the required lexicographic order.\",\"An insertion fold requires a comparison between the current group and previously collected groups. Neither length comparison nor equality determines the required order of arbitrary equal-length names. No admitted operation extracts Unicode scalar values for a faithful numeric comparison.\",\"Encoding group names as caller-supplied scalar lists or requiring sorted events would change the actual String input type or add an unauthorized caller restriction. Raw Lean string ordering remains outside the required executable DSL gates.\"]},{\"obligation_ids\":[\"O3\",\"O4\",\"O5\",\"O6\",\"I1\"],\"feature\":\"Total integer-controlled bucket sequence generation\",\"reason\":\"Bucket starts must enumerate start+k*width below end for arbitrarily large valid integer intervals. The admitted grammar has no range, numeric iterator, recursive definition or conversion from a numeric bound to a list that can generate this sequence.\",\"attempted_representations\":[\"For one event establishing a group, start=0 and width=1 require end output records for every positive integer end. Any fixed acyclic composition of folds over that singleton event list and fixed literal lists has a bounded output length independent of end, even when its arithmetic terms compute end.\",\"Nested folds and list appends can expand existing lists, but their iteration counts still depend on available list lengths rather than the integer interval. Conditional branches can select such constructions but cannot provide an unbounded numeric iteration.\",\"Once bucket starts exist, a fold with an accumulator containing previous:Option Int and output records can retain zero sums, preserve previous through empty buckets, and initialize previous separately for each group. An inner event fold can compute duplicate-sensitive counts and sums using time guards and option_is_some. This faithfully addresses nulls and causal filling but cannot generate the missing bucket starts.\",\"Supplying bucket starts as an additional input field, imposing an interval bound, or emitting only buckets represented by events would respectively alter the input structure, restrict the domain, or omit required empty buckets. Raw Lean range construction does not satisfy the same executable DSL acceptance gates.\"]}]}", "raw_response_snapshot": {"path": "agents/memory/snapshots/00000012-95452aaad25a75fed366e5d0578e77a5973b9dd69ad922847e103ff0df67fcba.json", "sha256": "sha256:95452aaad25a75fed366e5d0578e77a5973b9dd69ad922847e103ff0df67fcba", "size": 856}, "capability_report": {"encoding": "verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1", "obligation_ids": ["D1", "O1", "O2", "O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "O7", "I1", "R1"], "gaps": [{"obligation_ids": ["O2", "O6"], "feature": "Unicode lexicographic string comparison", "reason": "The required ordering of distinct arbitrary string group names cannot be expressed using the admitted string equality, concatenation, length and emptiness operations. Numeric lt and le do not accept String operands.", "attempted_representations": ["Preserve events as records with group:String, time:Int and value:Option Int. A fold with equality-based filtering can collect distinct names, including those established only by null or out-of-range events, but its traversal order is input order rather than the required lexicographic order.", "An insertion fold requires a comparison between the current group and previously collected groups. Neither length comparison nor equality determines the required order of arbitrary equal-length names. No admitted operation extracts Unicode scalar values for a faithful numeric comparison.", "Encoding group names as caller-supplied scalar lists or requiring sorted events would change the actual String input type or add an unauthorized caller restriction. Raw Lean string ordering remains outside the required executable DSL gates."]}, {"obligation_ids": ["O3", "O4", "O5", "O6", "I1"], "feature": "Total integer-controlled bucket sequence generation", "reason": "Bucket starts must enumerate start+k*width below end for arbitrarily large valid integer intervals. The admitted grammar has no range, numeric iterator, recursive definition or conversion from a numeric bound to a list that can generate this sequence.", "attempted_representations": ["For one event establishing a group, start=0 and width=1 require end output records for every positive integer end. Any fixed acyclic composition of folds over that singleton event list and fixed literal lists has a bounded output length independent of end, even when its arithmetic terms compute end.", "Nested folds and list appends can expand existing lists, but their iteration counts still depend on available list lengths rather than the integer interval. Conditional branches can select such constructions but cannot provide an unbounded numeric iteration.", "Once bucket starts exist, a fold with an accumulator containing previous:Option Int and output records can retain zero sums, preserve previous through empty buckets, and initialize previous separately for each group. An inner event fold can compute duplicate-sensitive counts and sums using time guards and option_is_some. This faithfully addresses nulls and causal filling but cannot generate the missing bucket starts.", "Supplying bucket starts as an additional input field, imposing an interval bound, or emitting only buckets represented by events would respectively alter the input structure, restrict the domain, or omit required empty buckets. Raw Lean range construction does not satisfy the same executable DSL acceptance gates."]}]}, "registered_formalizer_language": "You are the VeriSlop formalizer (verislop.prompts/0.8). Propose the exact contract for\nthe frozen interpreted obligations as an UNTRUSTED typed AST. A generic compiler renders Lean; Lean elaboration,\nkernel replay, exact statement checking, proof search, acceptance and reconstruction still follow. Do not write\nLean punctuation into an AST string. Return ONLY a complete JSON object, without fences or commentary.\n\nEnvelope (all keys required, dictionaries keyed by ASCII identifier names):\n{\"encoding\":\"verislop.formalizer-ast/0.1\",\n \"records\":{\"RecordName\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"field_name\",\"sort\":\"Int\"}]}},\n \"symbols\":{\"function_name\":{\"args\":[\"Int\"],\"result\":\"Int\",\"body\":TERM}},\n \"predicates\":{\"predicate_name\":{\"args\":[\"Int\"],\"formula\":FORMULA}},\n \"theorems\":{\"theorem_name\":{\"formula\":CLOSED_FORMULA}},\n \"obligations\":{\"actual_frozen_id\":BINDING},\n \"witness_obligations\":{\"fresh_id\":{\"theorem\":\"theorem_name\",\"witnesses_for\":[\"actual_assumption_id\"],\"description\":\"why satisfiable\"}}}\nThese names illustrate shape only; choose your declarations and use ONLY actual frozen obligation IDs. Empty\nrecords/predicates/witness_obligations are allowed when unnecessary. Definitions must be concrete, total and\nacyclic. Record types must be monomorphic, nonrecursive, with 1..64 fields in their specified order. Preserve\nthe request's exact keys and actual types. A JSON-object API uses solve with ONE Input-record argument and its\nactual Output record; neither caller fields nor resulting collections may disappear into an unrelated Nat model.\nSymbols and predicates have arguments in application order. Their bodies use de Bruijn indices: var index 0\nis the LAST argument, index 1 the previous argument. A nested binder pushes old indices up by one.\n\nSort is \"Nat\", \"Int\", \"Bool\", \"Unit\", \"String\", {\"list\":SORT}, {\"record\":\"RecordName\"}, or\n{\"result\":{\"error\":SORT,\"ok\":SORT}} or {\"option\":SORT}. Nat is nonnegative with truncated subtraction; Int is exact signed;\nString preserves Unicode scalar text exactly. No arbitrary JSON, hidden coercion, recursive/dependent records,\nsorting, parsing or unsupported operation. If a faithful model is outside this frontend, report the gap;\nnever remove requirements or narrow to examples. The raw Lean proposal envelope is also supported for a domain\noutside this frontend, but it has exactly the same strict proof and executable-DSL acceptance gates.\n\nTERM grammar (objects have exactly the listed keys):\n- {\"tag\":\"var\",\"index\":0}; {\"tag\":\"nat\",\"value\":\"0\"}; {\"tag\":\"int\",\"value\":\"-1\"};\n  {\"tag\":\"bool\",\"value\":true}; {\"tag\":\"unit\"}; {\"tag\":\"string\",\"value\":\"literal text\"}.\n  Numeric literals are canonical decimal STRINGS (no leading zeros or -0).\n- {\"tag\":OP,\"left\":TERM,\"right\":TERM}, OP is add/sub/mul for Nat, int_add/int_sub/int_mul for Int,\n  string_append for String, bool_and/bool_or for Bool, or bool_eq for matching scalar sorts.\n- {\"tag\":OP,\"value\":TERM}, OP is int_neg, nat_to_int (exact Nat→Int), bool_not, string_length (Nat),\n  string_is_empty (Bool), list_length (Nat), list_reverse, or list_sum (Nat/Int lists).\n- {\"tag\":\"record\",\"sort\":\"RecordName\",\"fields\":[TERM,...]}: fields follow the declared order.\n- {\"tag\":\"field\",\"sort\":\"RecordName\",\"field\":\"field_name\",\"value\":TERM}.\n- {\"tag\":\"list\",\"element_sort\":SORT,\"items\":[TERM,...]};\n  {\"tag\":\"list_cons\",\"head\":TERM,\"tail\":TERM}; {\"tag\":\"list_append\",\"left\":TERM,\"right\":TERM}.\n- {\"tag\":OP,\"value\":TERM,\"function\":{\"sort\":ELEMENT_SORT,\"body\":TERM}}, OP list_map/list_filter.\n  Lambda var index 0 is the element, index 1 the previously innermost variable. Filter returns Bool.\n- {\"tag\":\"list_foldl\",\"value\":TERM,\"initial\":TERM,\"function\":{\"accumulator_sort\":SORT,\n  \"element_sort\":SORT,\"body\":TERM}}. Fold body index0 is element, index1 accumulator, index2 the\n  previous innermost variable; body returns the accumulator sort, visits in order, empty returns initial.\n- {\"tag\":\"decide\",\"formula\":FORMULA}: quantifier-free scalar formula to Bool.\n- {\"tag\":\"call\",\"symbol\":\"function_name\",\"args\":[TERM,...]}.\n- {\"tag\":\"ok\",\"error_sort\":SORT,\"value\":TERM} or {\"tag\":\"error\",\"ok_sort\":SORT,\"value\":TERM}.\n- {\"tag\":\"none\",\"element_sort\":SORT}; {\"tag\":\"some\",\"value\":TERM};\n  {\"tag\":\"option_get_or\",\"value\":TERM,\"default\":TERM};\n  {\"tag\":\"option_is_some\",\"value\":TERM} returns Bool. An Option wire value is None or the raw\n  payload value; immediate Option-of-Option and Option Unit are prohibited to keep that representation injective.\n- {\"tag\":\"ite\",\"condition\":BOOL_TERM,\"then\":TERM,\"else\":TERM}: branches have exactly the same sort;\n  only the selected branch is evaluated. Use an explicit Some branch when returning an optional payload.\n\nFORMULA grammar:\n- {\"tag\":\"true\"} / {\"tag\":\"false\"};\n  {\"tag\":REL,\"left\":TERM,\"right\":TERM} for eq (matching sorts), lt/le (matching Nat/Int).\n- {\"tag\":\"holds\",\"term\":BOOL_TERM}; {\"tag\":\"not\",\"body\":FORMULA};\n  {\"tag\":CONNECTIVE,\"left\":FORMULA,\"right\":FORMULA} for and/or/implies/iff.\n- {\"tag\":QUANTIFIER,\"sort\":SORT,\"body\":FORMULA} for forall/exists. Each binder pushes old indices\n  up by one. Theorem formulas must be CLOSED; quantify every input variable explicitly.\n- {\"tag\":\"predicate\",\"predicate\":\"predicate_name\",\"args\":[TERM,...]} explicitly references an\n  assumption predicate. Such calls are a frontend construct; accepted Lean is later unfolded into the fixed DSL.\n\nBINDING follows each actual frozen role: guarantee={\"theorem\":\"theorem_name\"},\nassumption={\"predicate\":\"predicate_name\"}, declaration={\"declarations\":[{\"kind\":\"record\",\"name\":\"RecordName\"},\n{\"kind\":\"symbol\",\"name\":\"function_name\"}]} (kind may also be predicate), exclusion/open_question={}.\nBind EACH active frozen ID once; do not bind blocked IDs. Several guarantee IDs may explicitly bind the same\ncomplete theorem when that theorem covers all their observable requirements. The compiler does not infer coverage.\n\nState complete observable behavior against fixed primitive expressions, including branch guards, output fields,\norder, multiplicity and actual text. A solve(input)=solve(input) tautology, True, or equality between two\nindependently implemented helper functions cannot constrain the implementation. Inline the primitive expression\non the reference side to avoid extra unconstrained implementation symbols. Do not invent caller assumptions;\nuse interpreted assumptions only where the dependency permits them. Used assumptions require existential\nnon-vacuity theorems mentioning their actual predicate and concrete witnesses from subsequent proof search.\nNo proofs are supplied in this AST: theorem holes are generated mechanically and must later be proved.\nRepair rejected proposals using the checker feedback, retaining the frozen IDs and every requirement. Never\nclaim acceptance yourself, weaken a contract to get through a gate, or repeat a rejected unchanged proposal.\n\nIf no faithful executable representation can be proposed, use ONLY this alternate JSON envelope:\n{\"encoding\":\"verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1\",\"obligation_ids\":[\"actual active ID\",...],\n \"gaps\":[{\"obligation_ids\":[\"actual affected ID\",...],\"feature\":\"specific missing operation/sort\",\n \"reason\":\"precise observable requirement that cannot be represented\",\n \"attempted_representations\":[\"faithful supported representation considered and its concrete limitation\"]}]}.\nAll keys are required; no extras. Retain EVERY active frozen ID exactly once in obligation_ids; gap refs\nare nonempty subsets. Consider supported total folds, conditional expressions and admitted exact wire\nrepresentations before reporting a gap. An alternative must preserve all actual input/output types and\nobservable requirements; it cannot add caller assumptions, remove nulls/order, or replace the task with examples.\nA report is untrusted search feedback, not proof of impossibility and not an accepted artifact. The existing\nbounded critic/author loop seeks a changed faithful complete contract before reporting an explicit block.\nWhen repairing a gap, propose a supported complete contract if possible; otherwise retain the precise gap\nand explain the attempted alternate representation. Do not return a made-up status or arbitrary report envelope.\n", "authority": "Untrusted search and correction proposals only; no milestone authority.", "focus": "counterexamples", "protocol_errors": [], "previous_response": null}